course: dictionary
lesson: 975
title: Blush and the red face
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A blush is a red or pink colour that comes into your face. Context often shows you what it means. «Crushes are normal, and they often make people act strangely: staring, blushing, showing off or going quiet.» The list tells you blushing is something people do when they feel awkward or shy.
explain: «She blushed» in a story tells you her face went red because she felt shy or embarrassed. Blush can also be a noun. «A blush» is the red colour itself, and «blush makeup» is pink powder that people put on their cheeks.
explain: Blush is used in phrases too. «At first blush» means at first sight. Try it in the sentence: «At first blush, the plan looked perfect.» Does "At first sight, the plan looked perfect" still make sense? Yes, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Blush means to go red in the face because you feel shy, embarrassed or ashamed.
fact: A blush can also be a red or pink colour in the face, or a soft pink colour.
fact: «Blush makeup» means pink powder put on the cheeks.
fact: In science, a blush happens when stress chemicals like adrenaline widen the tiny blood vessels in the cheeks.
fact: «At first blush» means at first sight, and «spare someone's blushes» means save them from embarrassment (UK).
exercise: «She blushed when the whole class clapped for her.» What does blushed mean here? | She sang very loudly | She fell fast asleep | She ran out of the room | *She went red in the face because she felt shy or embarrassed
exercise: «At first blush, the plan looked perfect.» What does at first blush mean? | In a loud, angry voice | *At first sight | At the very last moment | After a long, long time
exercise: «His cheeks had a blush of pink after the joke.» What is a blush in this sentence? | A cold wind from the north | *A soft pink colour in the face | A type of warm bread | A loud, sudden noise
test: «Feeling nervous, blushing or shaking when you speak up is normal and does not make it any less brave.» What does this sentence say? | Blushing means you are telling a lie | Blushing means you are cross and must shout | *Blushing when you feel nervous is normal and does not make you less brave | Blushing means you cannot speak at all
test: Choose the meaning of blush in «blush makeup». | *Pink powder put on the cheeks | Cold water on the skin | A shy feeling inside | A loud sound
exam: «He blushed for pleasure at the old seaman's praise.» What caused the blush? | *Pleasure at the praise | Cold weather outside | Anger at a rude joke | Being very hungry
